==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|vitlauss}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*witjalausaz}}, whence also {{cog|en|witless}}. Composed of {{suffix|is|vit|gloss1=wits, intellect|laus|gloss2=[[-less]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈvɪht.løyːs/}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj/old|vitlausari|vitlausastur}}

# [[stupid]], [[foolish]]
#: {{syn|is|heimskur}}
#: {{ux|is|Mikið eru [[dúfa|dúfur]] '''vitlaus''' dýr.|Pigeons are such '''stupid''' animals.}}
# {{lb|is|informal}} [[insane]], [[crazy]]
#: {{syn|is|brjálaður|klikkaður|ruglaður|vitskertur}}
#: {{ux|is|Er allt orðið '''vitlaust''' hérna?|Has everything gone '''mad''' here?}}
# {{lb|is|colloquial}} [[wrong]], [[incorrect]]
#: {{syn|is|rangur|skakkur}}
#: {{ux|is|Þetta svar er '''vitlaust'''.|This answer is '''wrong'''.}}

